## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage without verification"**. Every production method is called (giving 95%+ line coverage), but almost nothing meaningful is asserted. Here's the breakdown:

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests That Verify Nothing

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | What Can Break Undetected |
|---|------|-------------|---------------------------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L17-21) | **No assertion at all** — fire-and-forget | `Save()` could silently drop products |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L33-36) | **No assertion** — calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the new price | Price logic `p.Price * (1 - fraction)` vs `newPrice` could be wrong |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L39-43) | **No assertion** — never verifies the product is gone | `Delete()` could be a no-op |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L63-66) | **No assertion, no setup** — doesn't even add products first | Count could return -1 and this passes |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68-74) | **No assertion** — the most complex logic in the class goes unverified | Discount formula could multiply instead of subtract |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85-88) | **No assertion** — never checks products were actually imported | Parsing bugs (wrong column order, decimal format) undetectable |

---

### 🟠 High — Weak Assertions (Assert-Not-Null on Non-Nullable Paths)

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Fix |
|---|------|-------------|-----|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L26-29) | `Assert.IsNotNull` only — never checks SKU, Name, or Price match | A method returning `new Product("","",0)` would pass |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` (L47-52) | `Assert.IsNotNull` on a `List<>` — lists are never null, only empty | Should assert `results.Count == 1` and verify correct product returned |
| 9 | `GetAllProducts_Works` (L55-60) | Same — `Assert.IsNotNull` on list | Should assert `all.Count == 1` |
| 10 | `ExportToCsv_Works` (L77-82) | `Assert.IsNotNull` on string — empty string passes | Should assert CSV content matches expected format |

---

### 🟡 Medium — Structural Issues

| # | Issue | Impact |
|---|-------|--------|
